==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Condemned Peng]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Kappy Jr.]] spawns as the boss.
**6 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**10 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**2 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
**2 [[Fallen Bear]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The strategy for the stage is simple. First stall for a while and use [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] to kill the first Doge Dark. Once you have enough cash, spam [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]
with [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel]] for the [[Fallen Bear]], [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Uril]] and [[Bowler Cat (Rare Cat)|Dodgeballer]] for everything else.

Any [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune unit]] that outranges Fallen Bear works well here, including [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]].

Note that Gato Amigo needs to be at least Lv.45 or have a Lv.6 HP Buff [[Talents|Talent]] to survive 2 hits from [[Diabrollow]]'s [[Mini-Wave]]s. Otherwise bring [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to help against them.

==Trivia==
*According to this stage's Japanese name, the "Long and Short" are the hands on a clock.
*Since [[Diabrollow]] appears to be based on the Greek Titan [[wikipedia:Cronus|Cronus]], its presence in Meeting of Long and Short may be a reference to how Cronus is often confused with [[wikipedia:Chronos|Chronos]], the Greek god of time.

